<?xml version="1.0" encoding="utf-8"?>
<!--
  Resource-shrinker keeps for the sdp/ssp dimension tables.

  Nothing references these by id. `:core:designsystem`'s `dimen/Sdp.kt` builds the resource *name*
  at runtime — "_8sdp" — and hands it to `Resources.getIdentifier`, so the shrinker sees no
  reference to any of the ~660 dimens and strips the lot. Sdp.kt caches the resolved id per process,
  but that is a speed fix and changes nothing here: the lookup is still by name, and a name is not
  something the shrinker can follow.

  It does not crash when that happens, which is the dangerous part: `Int.sdp` falls back to plain
  `dp` on a zero id, so the app keeps running and quietly renders every dimension as raw dp with no
  screen scaling at all. Correct on one handset, wrong on every other.

  Because the failure reports itself in no other way, the check lives in CI: `ci.yml` counts the
  `_Nsdp` dimensions in the built release APK with `aapt2 dump resources` and fails below 600. Only
  the APK can answer that question — the app launching proves nothing.

  This stays for as long as sizes are resolved by name. See the shrinking section in CLAUDE.md.
-->
<resources
    xmlns:tools="http://schemas.android.com/tools"
    tools:keep="@dimen/_*sdp,@dimen/_*ssp" />
